--- typeof -- type coercion, predicates, and utility functions for the handl runtime.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `typeof` stdlib interface: 13 functions
--- and 12 type-tag constants covering coercion, type predicates, and
--- utilities. The Rust bridge in `plugin-lib-utils` loads this file via
--- `include_str!`, parses the `cap` declarations for the plugin capability
--- surface, and registers the Rust handls (handlers) in an `OpRegistry`
--- that dispatches each `op` to its native Rust impl.
---
--- Note: the module was originally named `type`, but `type` became a keyword
--- in v0.1 (ADR-0074), so the module was renamed to `typeof` to avoid the
--- conflict. The function `typeof.type_of(v)` is the primary type-checking
--- function used in handl source files.
---
--- All functions are FFI atoms (they call Rust type-checking and coercion
--- logic that cannot be expressed as pure handl arrows without losing the
--- exact error messages the tests rely on). The `op`/`handl` declaration
--- form (ADR-0077 Phase 2) declares the interface; the Rust `Function`
--- impls in `ops.rs` provide the logic.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- typeof.string -- the type.string tag constant.
--- typeof.str -- the type.str tag constant.
--- typeof.number -- the type.number tag constant.
--- typeof.num -- the type.num tag constant.
--- typeof.bool -- the type.bool tag constant.
--- typeof.null -- the type.null tag constant.
--- typeof.array -- the type.array tag constant.
--- typeof.arr -- the type.arr tag constant.
--- typeof.object -- the type.object tag constant.
--- typeof.obj -- the type.obj tag constant.
--- typeof.any -- the type.any tag constant.
--- typeof.unknown -- the type.unknown tag constant.
--- typeof.is -- test whether a value matches a kind.
--- typeof.must -- strict projection: wrap the result in an ok/err record.
--- typeof.may -- potential extraction: extract the matching component or null.
--- typeof.not -- complement: extract the non-matching component or null.
--- typeof.when -- conditional: extract the matching component or return a default.
--- typeof.to_string -- coerce a value to a string.
--- typeof.to_number -- coerce a value to a number.
--- typeof.to_bool -- coerce a value to a boolean.
--- typeof.type_of -- get the type name of a value.
--- typeof.typeof -- alias for type_of.
--- typeof.identity -- return the value unchanged.
--- typeof.default -- return the value if non-null, otherwise a fallback.
--- typeof.coalesce -- return the first non-null value from a list of arguments.
cap "typeof.string"
cap "typeof.str"
cap "typeof.number"
cap "typeof.num"
cap "typeof.bool"
cap "typeof.null"
cap "typeof.array"
cap "typeof.arr"
cap "typeof.object"
cap "typeof.obj"
cap "typeof.any"
cap "typeof.unknown"
cap "typeof.is"
cap "typeof.must"
cap "typeof.may"
cap "typeof.not"
cap "typeof.when"
cap "typeof.to_string"
cap "typeof.to_number"
cap "typeof.to_bool"
cap "typeof.type_of"
cap "typeof.typeof"
cap "typeof.identity"
cap "typeof.default"
cap "typeof.coalesce"
